6 = 48. Write down the result in the thousands place of the product.\n\n9. **Multiply the hundreds place**: Multiply the hundreds digit of the first number (2) by the hundreds digit of the second number (6). This gives us 2 * 6 = 12. Write down the result in the thousands place of the product.\n\nNow, add all the partial products together:.\n\n```.\n  281.\n× 641.\n-----.\n  281  (1 * 1).\n  1688  (8 * 1 + 1 * 4).\n 16880  (2 * 1 + 8 * 4 + 1 * 6).\n168800  (2 * 4 + 8 * 6 + 1 * 12).\n1688000 (2 * 6).\n-----. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
